Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:25:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] News Site as a site of the Home Page server:
 newsreader.hosting.site hands the app under /news with its preview and
 version to the server that now owns port 5000 on this PC, which turns News
 Site's own start at logon off; run on its own, News Site serves itself under
 /news with "/" leading there

On this PC the Home Page project (~/Documents/Claude/Home Page) owns the address: its
server listens on port 5000 (Tailscale, LAN, loopback for Funnel), lists the sites on "/"
and serves CoreLab under /infra. It loads News Site through sites.toml
(python = "../News Site/work/app", entry = "newsreader.hosting:site") and restarts into
new code when VERSION changes, reinstalling packages when requirements.txt changed.

- newsreader/hosting.py: site(mount, host) -> the WSGI app, name, subtitle, preview()
  (moved here from the portal, now with a heading), disallow, legacy, version(); trusts
  the host's names; records where it is served; writes instance/hosted.json and turns
  News Site's start at logon off (removing its task) so the two never race for the port.
- newsreader/portal: only News Site on its own (another PC, a test build): /news, "/"
  and old addresses redirect there, /relay/ answered in place, public name https+noindex.
  The front page (index.html, portal.css, CoreLab serving) moved to the Home Page.
- launcher.py: while the Home Page server answers for this copy (hosted.json), opening
  the launcher opens the site there instead of starting a second server; the logon start
  does nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
